{% doc %}
  blocks/_showcase-video.liquid — private to `blocks/_showcase-column.liquid`.

  One video review: a face, a play control, and what they said written over the
  foot of their own photograph.

  ## The card is one box, not a picture with a caption under it

  `.showcase-card` is a one-cell grid and everything in it occupies that cell —
  the photograph, the scrim over it, and the words. The row is as tall as the
  taller of the two, so a long quote grows the card and stretches the picture
  with it rather than spilling off the bottom of a fixed frame.

  That is why the ratio is on the media rather than on the card. A card with
  `aspect-ratio` on itself is a box that ignores its own contents; a media cell
  with one is a *preferred* height that the grid row is free to beat.

  ## Nothing is fetched for a video nobody opens

  The card carries a `<template>` holding a whole `<deferred-media>` — poster,
  play control, and a second `<template>` with the real video or embed. Markup
  inside a template is inert: no fetch, no decode, no metadata request. A lane
  of twelve reviews costs twelve posters' worth of `<img>` and nothing else
  until one is pressed, at which point
  `assets/testimonial-showcase.js` clones that template into the section's
  modal.

  Two templates rather than one because they switch off two different things.
  The outer one keeps the modal's poster out of the page; the inner one is
  `<deferred-media>`'s own contract, and keeps the video out of the modal until
  the play badge is pressed there too.

  ## The play control is a button, and the card is not a link

  A card that navigates cannot also open a video without the first tap doing
  something nobody asked for. So the picture is not a link, the play control is
  a `<button>`, and it carries the reviewer's name as its accessible label —
  "Play Myrna T.'s video" rather than twelve buttons all called "Play".

  The lanes clone their cards to loop, so the button's handler is delegated from
  the section rather than bound here: a listener attached at build time would be
  missing from every copy, which is most of what is on the screen.

  ## The verified seal is drawn here rather than in `snippets/icon.liquid`

  It is two shapes that have to sit inside each other — a scalloped disc and the
  tick on it — and the icon snippet renders one path with one stroke. Adding a
  case for it would mean either a seal with no tick or a second icon that only
  makes sense stacked on the first.

  ## Three copies of every default

  The schema default, the `| default:` beside the setting that reads it, and the
  column preset in the section. They have to agree: a card created from a preset
  that omits a setting has nothing stored, so it falls through to the Liquid
  fallback while the editor panel shows the schema's number.
{% enddoc %}

{%- liquid
  assign s = block.settings

  comment
    ---- what there is to play ----

    A hosted video is a file in Shopify's CDN — real playback control, real
    posters, `video_tag` writing the sources. A URL is YouTube or Vimeo and an
    iframe. Both are supported because merchants have their footage in both
    places, and the hosted path is better in every measurable way.

    Truthiness for the object and `''` for the string: nil is falsy in every
    Liquid engine, and `nil != blank` is not consistently false in all of them.
    That difference decides whether a merchant with only a URL gets an embed or
    an empty `<video>`.
  endcomment
  assign hosted = false
  if s.video
    assign hosted = true
  endif

  assign external = s.video_url | default: ''

  assign has_video = false
  if hosted or external != ''
    assign has_video = true
  endif

  comment
    The card's own picture, and the modal's poster, are the same image resolved
    once. A merchant who uploads a video gets its `preview_image` without being
    asked for a still; picking one overrides it, which is worth doing when the
    first frame is a fade from black.
  endcomment
  assign poster = s.image
  if poster == blank and hosted
    assign poster = s.video.preview_image
  endif

  assign author = s.author | default: ''
  assign rating = s.rating | default: 5 | plus: 0

  assign show_verified = s.show_verified
  if show_verified == nil
    assign show_verified = true
  endif

  comment
    The button says whose video it is. Twelve buttons called "Play" is twelve
    identical stops in a screen reader's list of controls, and the name is the
    only thing that tells them apart.
  endcomment
  assign play_label = 'sections.testimonials_showcase.play_video' | t
  if author != ''
    assign play_label = 'sections.testimonials_showcase.play_video_by' | t: name: author
  endif

  comment
    ---- the frame ----

    The theme's border group, resolved exactly as `blocks/_testimonial-card.liquid`
    resolves its own, with one addition: Gradient. The design draws a stroke that
    is bright at one corner and gone at the other, which a single border colour
    cannot express — so that option paints a gradient into a pseudo-element and
    masks its middle out, and the plain styles keep using a real border.

    A blank colour has no alpha channel to read until the scheme resolves in the
    browser, so `color_modify` cannot fade it and `color-mix` does that job at
    paint time instead.
  endcomment
  assign border_line = s.border_style | default: 'gradient'
  assign border_width = 0
  assign border_paint = ''

  if border_line != 'none'
    assign border_width = s.border_width | default: 1 | plus: 0

    assign border_percent = s.border_opacity | default: 100 | plus: 0
    if s.border_color == blank
      assign border_paint = 'color-mix(in srgb, currentColor ' | append: border_percent | append: '%, transparent)'
    else
      assign border_alpha = border_percent | divided_by: 100.0
      assign border_paint = s.border_color | color_modify: 'alpha', border_alpha
    endif
  endif

  assign gradient_paint = ''
  if border_line == 'gradient'
    assign gradient_angle = s.border_gradient_angle | default: 200 | plus: 0
    assign gradient_end = s.border_color_end | default: 'rgba(255,255,255,0)'
    assign gradient_paint = 'linear-gradient(' | append: gradient_angle | append: 'deg, ' | append: border_paint | append: ', ' | append: gradient_end | append: ')'
  endif

  assign radius = s.border_radius | default: 20 | plus: 0
  assign radius_mobile = s.border_radius_mobile | default: radius | plus: 0

  comment
    ---- the scrim ----

    A gradient rather than a flat tint, and a height rather than a full cover:
    the words need a dark floor to sit on and the face above them does not need
    dimming. `--sv-scrim-height` is where the gradient starts, as a share of the
    card.
  endcomment
  assign scrim_paint = ''
  if s.scrim_color != blank
    assign scrim_alpha = s.scrim_opacity | default: 90 | plus: 0
    assign scrim_alpha = scrim_alpha | divided_by: 100.0
    assign scrim_paint = s.scrim_color | color_modify: 'alpha', scrim_alpha
  endif

  assign scrim_height = s.scrim_height | default: 62 | plus: 0

  comment
    ---- the play control ----

    Sized from one number. The glyph, the disc and the ring around it are all
    derived from `play_size`, so a merchant moves one slider rather than three
    that can be set out of proportion with each other.
  endcomment
  comment
    Resolved here rather than in the `render` argument: filters are not allowed
    on arguments passed to `render`, and the tag fails to parse rather than
    ignoring them.
  endcomment
  assign star_size = s.star_size | default: 11 | plus: 0

  assign play_size = s.play_size | default: 48 | plus: 0
  assign play_glyph = play_size | times: 0.36 | round
  if play_glyph < 8
    assign play_glyph = 8
  endif

  assign card_ratio = s.card_ratio | default: '3-4'

  comment
    `sizes` describes the widest this card is ever painted. A lane is a column
    about a third of the row on a desktop and a fixed-width card on a phone, so
    a wrong hint here is a photograph arriving three sizes larger than the box
    it fills — once per card, and the lanes clone their cards.
  endcomment
  assign card_sizes = '(min-width: 990px) 360px, (min-width: 750px) 320px, 80vw'

  assign card_classes = 'showcase-card'
  if border_line == 'gradient'
    assign card_classes = card_classes | append: ' showcase-card--gradient-border'
  endif
  unless has_video
    assign card_classes = card_classes | append: ' showcase-card--still'
  endunless
-%}

{%- capture card_style -%}
  {%- render 'spacing', block: s, declarations: true -%}
  --sv-card-radius: {{ radius }}px;
  --sv-card-radius-mobile: {{ radius_mobile }}px;
  --sv-card-gap: {{ s.gap | default: 8 | plus: 0 }}px;
  --sv-card-ratio: {% render 'aspect-ratio', ratio: card_ratio, image: poster %};
  --sv-scrim-height: {{ scrim_height }}%;
  --sv-play-size: {{ play_size }}px;
  --sv-name-size: {{ s.name_size | default: 18 | plus: 0 }}px;
  --sv-headline-size: {{ s.headline_size | default: 15 | plus: 0 }}px;
  --sv-quote-size: {{ s.quote_size | default: 15 | plus: 0 }}px;
  {%- if border_width > 0 -%}
    --sv-card-border-width: {{ border_width }}px;
    {%- if border_line == 'gradient' -%}
      --sv-card-border-image: {{ gradient_paint }};
    {%- else -%}
      --sv-card-border-style: {{ border_line }};
      --sv-card-border-color: {{ border_paint }};
    {%- endif -%}
  {%- endif -%}
  {%- if s.glow_size > 0 and s.glow_color != blank -%}
    --sv-card-glow: 0 0 {{ s.glow_size | plus: 0 }}px {{ s.glow_color }};
  {%- endif -%}
  {%- if scrim_paint != '' -%}
    --sv-scrim: {{ scrim_paint }};
  {%- endif -%}
  {%- if s.text_color != blank -%}
    --sv-card-text: {{ s.text_color }};
  {%- endif -%}
  {%- if s.star_color != blank -%}
    --sv-star-color: {{ s.star_color }};
  {%- endif -%}
  {%- if s.verified_color != blank -%}
    --sv-verified: {{ s.verified_color }};
  {%- endif -%}
  {%- if s.play_background != blank -%}
    --sv-play-background: {{ s.play_background }};
  {%- endif -%}
  {%- if s.play_icon_color != blank -%}
    --sv-play-icon: {{ s.play_icon_color }};
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endcapture -%}

<article
  class="{{ card_classes }}"
  data-showcase-card
  {%- if author != blank %} data-showcase-label="{{ author | escape }}"{% endif %}
  style="{{ card_style | strip_newlines | strip }}"
  {{ block.shopify_attributes }}
>
  <div class="showcase-card__media">
    {% render 'image',
       image: poster,
       alt: '',
       ratio: card_ratio,
       class: 'showcase-card__image',
       wrapper_class: 'showcase-card__frame',
       placeholder: 'hero-apparel-2',
       sizes: card_sizes %}
  </div>

  {%- comment -%}
    Decoration, and it says so. The words above it are the content and the
    gradient exists so they can be read over a photograph nobody chose for its
    contrast.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <span class="showcase-card__scrim" aria-hidden="true"></span>

  {%- if has_video -%}
    <button
      type="button"
      class="showcase-card__play"
      data-showcase-play
      aria-label="{{ play_label | escape }}"
    >
      <span class="showcase-card__play-glyph" aria-hidden="true">
        {% render 'icon', icon: 'play', size: play_glyph %}
      </span>
    </button>
  {%- endif -%}

  {%- comment -%}
    `data-block-spacing` is on the body rather than on the card, and that is not
    a mistake. The four padding sliders are the room around the *words*; the
    card itself is a photograph that runs to its own corners, and padding on it
    would inset the picture instead.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <div class="showcase-card__body" data-block-spacing>
    {%- if author != blank or rating > 0 -%}
      <div class="showcase-card__head">
        {%- if author != blank -%}
          <span class="showcase-card__identity">
            {%- if show_verified -%}
              {%- comment -%}
                A seal, not a claim. The word "Verified" is not written out here
                because the design has no room for it beside the name — so it is
                `aria-hidden` and the sentence that carries the meaning is the
                one on the button and in the quote itself.
              {%- endcomment -%}
              <svg
                class="showcase-card__seal"
                viewBox="0 0 24 24"
                fill="none"
                aria-hidden="true"
                focusable="false"
              >
                <path
                  d="M12 1.2l2.1 2.1 2.9-.4.9 2.8 2.8.9-.4 2.9 2.1 2.1-2.1 2.1.4 2.9-2.8.9-.9 2.8-2.9-.4L12 22.8l-2.1-2.1-2.9.4-.9-2.8-2.8-.9.4-2.9L1.6 12.4l2.1-2.1-.4-2.9 2.8-.9.9-2.8 2.9.4L12 1.2z"
                  fill="currentColor"
                />
                <path
                  d="M8.4 12.2l2.5 2.5 4.7-5"
                  stroke="var(--sv-verified-check, #0F2E2F)"
                  stroke-width="2"
                  stroke-linecap="round"
                  stroke-linejoin="round"
                />
              </svg>
            {%- endif -%}
            <cite class="showcase-card__name">{{ author | escape }}</cite>
          </span>
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- if rating > 0 -%}
          <span class="showcase-card__rating">
            {% render 'rating-stars', rating: rating, size: star_size %}
          </span>
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- if s.headline != blank -%}
      <p class="showcase-card__headline">{{ s.headline | escape }}</p>
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- if s.quote != blank -%}
      <blockquote class="showcase-card__quote">{{ s.quote }}</blockquote>
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>

  {%- if has_video -%}
    {%- comment -%}
      The modal's contents, held inert until the play control is pressed.

      Both the outer element and the inner one are templates and they switch off
      two different things — see the note at the head of this file. Cloning the
      outer one puts a `<deferred-media>` in the modal with a poster and nothing
      loaded; pressing that poster is what fetches the footage.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <template data-showcase-video>
      <deferred-media class="showcase-media" data-autoplay="false">
        <button
          type="button"
          class="showcase-media__poster"
          data-ref="poster"
          aria-label="{{ play_label | escape }}"
        >
          {% render 'image',
             image: poster,
             alt: '',
             ratio: '16-9',
             class: 'showcase-media__image',
             placeholder: 'hero-apparel-2',
             sizes: '(min-width: 990px) 880px, 100vw' %}

          {%- comment -%}
            The rotating badge. The ring of text is one `textPath` around a
            circle rather than letters positioned one at a time, so it stays
            legible at any size and a merchant can write their own words into
            it. It spins in CSS and stops under `prefers-reduced-motion`.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          <span class="showcase-media__badge" aria-hidden="true">
            <svg class="showcase-media__badge-ring" viewBox="0 0 100 100" focusable="false">
              <defs>
                <path
                  id="showcase-badge-path-{{ block.id }}"
                  d="M50,50 m-34,0 a34,34 0 1,1 68,0 a34,34 0 1,1 -68,0"
                  fill="none"
                />
              </defs>
              <text class="showcase-media__badge-text">
                <textPath href="#showcase-badge-path-{{ block.id }}" startOffset="0">
                  {{- 'sections.testimonials_showcase.badge' | t -}}
                </textPath>
              </text>
            </svg>
            <span class="showcase-media__badge-glyph">
              {% render 'icon', icon: 'play', size: 22 %}
            </span>
          </span>
        </button>

        <template data-ref="template">
          {%- if hosted -%}
            {{ s.video
               | video_tag:
                   autoplay: true,
                   loop: false,
                   muted: false,
                   controls: true,
                   playsinline: true,
                   preload: 'none',
                   image_size: '1280x',
                   class: 'showcase-media__player' }}
          {%- else -%}
            {%- comment -%}
              `external_video_url` builds the embed with the flags a review needs
              — it starts on press, it does not trail into unrelated videos, and
              it carries no channel branding. It is deliberately *not* muted:
              somebody pressing play on a testimonial is there for what the
              person says.
            {%- endcomment -%}
            {{ external
               | external_video_url:
                   autoplay: true,
                   loop: false,
                   controls: true,
                   playsinline: true,
                   modestbranding: true,
                   rel: 0
               | external_video_tag:
                   class: 'showcase-media__player',
                   loading: 'lazy',
                   title: play_label }}
          {%- endif -%}
        </template>
      </deferred-media>
    </template>
  {%- endif -%}
</article>

{%- comment -%}
  Every setting below is a control a merchant reaches in the editor, and the
  schema is one element's styling surface: splitting it to get under Theme
  Check's count of 40 would split the thing the settings style.
{%- endcomment -%}
{% # theme-check-disable ExcessiveSettingsCount %}
{% schema %}
{
  "name": "t:blocks.showcase_video.name",
  "tag": null,
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "t:blocks.showcase_video.paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "video",
      "id": "video",
      "label": "t:shared.background.video.label",
      "info": "t:blocks.showcase_video.settings.video.info"
    },
    {
      "type": "video_url",
      "id": "video_url",
      "label": "t:shared.background.video_url.label",
      "info": "t:shared.background.video_url.info",
      "accept": ["youtube", "vimeo"]
    },
    {
      "type": "image_picker",
      "id": "image",
      "label": "t:blocks.showcase_video.settings.image.label",
      "info": "t:blocks.showcase_video.settings.image.info"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "author",
      "label": "t:blocks.testimonial.settings.author.label",
      "default": "Myrna T."
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "show_verified",
      "label": "t:blocks.showcase_video.settings.show_verified.label",
      "info": "t:blocks.showcase_video.settings.show_verified.info",
      "default": true
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "rating",
      "label": "t:blocks.testimonial.settings.rating.label",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 5,
      "step": 1,
      "default": 5
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "headline",
      "label": "t:blocks.showcase_video.settings.headline.label",
      "info": "t:blocks.showcase_video.settings.headline.info",
      "default": "95% love their experience"
    },
    {
      "type": "richtext",
      "id": "quote",
      "label": "t:blocks.testimonial.settings.quote.label",
      "default": "<p>“I used to crash after lunch, but now my energy stays stable. It’s such an easy habit.”</p>"
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "t:blocks.showcase_video.headers.shape"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "card_ratio",
      "label": "t:shared.image_ratio.label",
      "info": "t:blocks.showcase_video.settings.card_ratio.info",
      "options": [
        { "value": "9-16", "label": "t:shared.image_ratio.options__1.label" },
        { "value": "2-3", "label": "t:shared.image_ratio.options__2.label" },
        { "value": "3-4", "label": "t:shared.image_ratio.options__3.label" },
        { "value": "portrait", "label": "t:shared.image_ratio.options__4.label" },
        { "value": "1-1", "label": "t:shared.image_ratio.options__5.label" },
        { "value": "4-3", "label": "t:shared.image_ratio.options__6.label" },
        { "value": "16-9", "label": "t:shared.image_ratio.options__7.label" }
      ],
      "default": "3-4"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "border_radius",
      "label": "t:shared.corner_radius.label",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 48,
      "step": 2,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 20
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "border_radius_mobile",
      "label": "t:blocks.showcase_video.settings.border_radius_mobile.label",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 48,
      "step": 2,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 16
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "gap",
      "label": "t:shared.gap.label",
      "info": "t:blocks.showcase_video.settings.gap.info",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 32,
      "step": 1,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 8
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "border_style",
      "label": "t:blocks.group.settings.border_style.label",
      "info": "t:blocks.showcase_video.settings.border_style.info",
      "options": [
        { "value": "none", "label": "t:shared.options.none" },
        { "value": "solid", "label": "t:shared.options.solid" },
        { "value": "dashed", "label": "t:shared.options.dashed" },
        { "value": "gradient", "label": "t:blocks.showcase_video.settings.border_style.options__4.label" }
      ],
      "default": "gradient"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "border_width",
      "label": "t:shared.border.thickness.label",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 6,
      "step": 1,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 1,
      "visible_if": "{{ block.settings.border_style != 'none' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "border_opacity",
      "label": "t:shared.border.opacity.label",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 100,
      "step": 5,
      "unit": "%",
      "default": 100,
      "visible_if": "{{ block.settings.border_style != 'none' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "color",
      "id": "border_color",
      "label": "t:blocks.group.settings.border_color.label",
      "default": "#03D26F",
      "visible_if": "{{ block.settings.border_style != 'none' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "color",
      "id": "border_color_end",
      "label": "t:blocks.showcase_video.settings.border_color_end.label",
      "info": "t:blocks.showcase_video.settings.border_color_end.info",
      "default": "#0F2E2F",
      "visible_if": "{{ block.settings.border_style == 'gradient' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "border_gradient_angle",
      "label": "t:blocks.showcase_video.settings.border_gradient_angle.label",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 360,
      "step": 5,
      "unit": "deg",
      "default": 200,
      "visible_if": "{{ block.settings.border_style == 'gradient' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "color",
      "id": "glow_color",
      "label": "t:blocks.showcase_video.settings.glow_color.label",
      "info": "t:blocks.showcase_video.settings.glow_color.info",
      "default": "rgba(3, 210, 111, 0.25)"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "glow_size",
      "label": "t:blocks.showcase_video.settings.glow_size.label",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 60,
      "step": 2,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 24
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "t:blocks.showcase_video.headers.overlay"
    },
    {
      "type": "color",
      "id": "scrim_color",
      "label": "t:blocks.showcase_video.settings.scrim_color.label",
      "info": "t:blocks.showcase_video.settings.scrim_color.info",
      "default": "#0F2E2F"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "scrim_opacity",
      "label": "t:blocks.showcase_video.settings.scrim_opacity.label",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 100,
      "step": 5,
      "unit": "%",
      "default": 90
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "scrim_height",
      "label": "t:blocks.showcase_video.settings.scrim_height.label",
      "info": "t:blocks.showcase_video.settings.scrim_height.info",
      "min": 20,
      "max": 100,
      "step": 2,
      "unit": "%",
      "default": 62
    },
    {
      "type": "color",
      "id": "text_color",
      "label": "t:blocks.showcase_video.settings.text_color.label",
      "default": "#FFFFFF"
